-- title:
--   One-sided pool from level polynomials on the X₁(Mp) model
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$, a non-zero natural number $M$ with $5 \le M$ and $p \nmid M$, a field $L$ of characteristic zero which is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of type $\{p\}$, and an element $\zeta \in L$ that is a primitive $p$-th root of unity. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L \subseteq L((q))$ (Laurent series over $L$) which, by the hypothesis `hK`, equals [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.x1FunctionField (M * p))`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), i.e. the $L$-subfield of $L((q))$ generated by the image, under the coefficientwise embedding [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81) of $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ into $L((q))$, of the $q$-expansion function field of level $\Gamma_1(Mp)$ over $\mathbb{Q}$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with $L$ as fraction field, such that the image of $p$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$ (`hAp`) and $\zeta$ lies in the image of $A$ in $L$ (`hζA`), and let $K$ carry an $A$-algebra structure compatible with the tower $A \to L \to K$. Let $j \in K$ be a non-zero element whose image in $L((q))$ is [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81), the $q$-expansion of the modular $j$-invariant.
--
--   Write $X :=$ [`ModularCurve.TwoChartModel A K j`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L229) for the two-chart model, the pushout of the two morphisms `fFin`, `fInf` out of the middle chart, its charts being the spectra of the subalgebras of $K$ of elements integral over $A[j]$ and over $A[j^{-1}]$ respectively, and write $c :=$ [`ModularCurve.TwoChart.modelTo A K j`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L252) $: X \to \operatorname{Spec} A$ for its structure morphism. Let $U$ be an open subscheme of $X$ such that $U \hookrightarrow X \to \operatorname{Spec} A$ is smooth of relative dimension $1$, and assume (`hUmax`) that $U$ contains every open $W$ of $X$ with the same property. Let $\varepsilon$ be a section of $c$ (an element of `SchemeHomOver (𝟙 (Spec A)) c`, that is a morphism $\operatorname{Spec} A \to X$ whose composite with $c$ is the identity) whose set-theoretic image lies in $U$ (`hε`), let $\sigma$ be an automorphism of $X$ with $\sigma$ followed by $c$ equal to $c$ (`hσ`), and let $\varepsilon'$ be a further section of $c$ with $\varepsilon$ followed by $\sigma$ equal to $\varepsilon'$ (`hε'`).
--
--   The far-side hypothesis `hfar` requires the following for every $f \in A$, every algebraically closed field $k$ and every morphism $s : \operatorname{Spec} k \to \operatorname{Spec} A_f$, where $A_f$ denotes the localisation of $A$ away from $f$: if the geometric fibre, i.e. the second projection of the pullback of the base-changed curve $X_{A_f} \to \operatorname{Spec} A_f$ along $s$, is not smooth, then (i) every point $y$ of that fibre lying in the connected component, inside the trace of $U$ on the fibre (the preimage of $U$ along the first projection of the fibre followed by the first projection of $X_{A_f}$), of the point of the fibre determined by $\varepsilon$ (the image of the closed point of $\operatorname{Spec} k$ under `sectionFibrePoint (sectionBaseChange (Localization.Away f) ε) s`) is carried by the endomorphism of the fibre induced by `curveChange σ.hom hσ (specMap A (Localization.Away f))` into the trace of $U$ with that connected component removed, and (ii) the point of the fibre determined by $\varepsilon'$ lies in the trace of $U$ with that connected component removed.
--
--   Let $v$ be an element of [`ModularCurve.TwoChart.chartAlgFin A K j`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L135), the subalgebra of $K$ consisting of the elements integral over $A[j]$. The dictionary hypothesis `hdict` requires: for every algebraically closed field $k$ and every non-injective ring homomorphism $\varphi : A \to k$, every point $\mathfrak{q}$ of the finite chart $\operatorname{Spec}(\mathrm{chartAlgFin})$ with $v \notin \mathfrak{q}$, and every point $y$ of the pullback of $c$ along $\operatorname{Spec}\varphi$ whose image under the first projection is the image of $\mathfrak{q}$ under the chart inclusion [`ModularCurve.TwoChart.ιFin A K j`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L231), the point $y$ lies in the preimage of $U$ under the first projection and, moreover, in the connected component of that preimage containing the point determined by $\varepsilon$ over $\operatorname{Spec} k$.
--
--   Finally, let $A_0, B_0, n_0, b, M_b$ be natural numbers with $A_0 b^{n_0} + B_0 + 1 < M_b$, let $g : \operatorname{Fin} M_b \to \mathbb{Z}[X]$ be a family of monic polynomials and $rk : \operatorname{Fin} M_b \to \mathbb{N}$, and assume for each $i$ that the quotient of `chartAlgFin` by the ideal generated by $g_i(v)$ (the image `Polynomial.aeval v (g i)`) is a finite $A$-module, étale over $A$, free over $A$, of $A$-rank $rk_i$, with $1 \le rk_i \le b$; assume further that the ideals generated by $g_i(v)$ and $g_{i'}(v)$ are comaximal for $i \ne i'$ (`hcop`) and that the ideal generated by $g_i(v)$ together with the ideal generated by $v$ is the unit ideal, for every $i$ (`hcopv`).
--
--   The conclusion is a chain of existential binders with trivial body `True`, so that all its content is carried by the binders; note that the naturals $b$ and $M_b$ are re-bound there, so the data produced are governed by fresh $b$ and $M_b$. It asserts the existence of: an element $f \in A$ not lying in the maximal ideal of $A$; natural numbers $b$ and $M_b$ with $A_0 b^{n_0} + B_0 < M_b$; a commutative ring $R'$ which is an algebra over $A$ and over $A_f$, compatibly with the tower $A \to A_f \to R'$, and which is finite, étale and faithfully flat over $A_f$; a family $B : \operatorname{Fin} M_b \to \mathrm{Type}$ of commutative $A_f$-algebras, each finite and étale over $A_f$; degrees $\deg_i$ with $1 \le \deg_i \le b$ for all $i$; $R'$-algebra isomorphisms $\varphi_i : R' \otimes_{A_f} B_i \cong (\operatorname{Fin}(\deg i) \to R')$; and morphisms $z_i : \operatorname{Spec} B_i \to X_{A_f}$ into the pullback of $c$ along $\operatorname{Spec} A_f \to \operatorname{Spec} A$, subject to the following conditions: each $z_i$ is a closed immersion; $z_i$ followed by the structure morphism `baseChange A c (Localization.Away f)` equals `specMap (Localization.Away f) (B i)`; the image of each $z_i$ lies in the preimage of $U$ under the first projection of $X_{A_f}$; the images of the $z_i$ are pairwise disjoint; for every algebraically closed field $k$, every $s : \operatorname{Spec} k \to \operatorname{Spec} A_f$ and every $i$, the preimage under the first projection of the geometric fibre of the image of $z_i$ is contained in the connected component, inside the trace of $U$ on that fibre, of the point determined by $\varepsilon$; the image of each $z_i$ is disjoint from the image of the base-changed section `sectionBaseChange (Localization.Away f) ε`; the image of each $z_i$ is disjoint from the image of the base-changed section `sectionBaseChange (Localization.Away f) ε'`; and for all indices $i$ and $j$ (not only distinct ones), the image of $z_i$ is disjoint from the image of $z_j$ followed by `curveChange σ.hom hσ (specMap A (Localization.Away f))`, the base change of $\sigma$ to $X_{A_f}$.
--
--   This is the assembly step that converts level polynomials in a chart element $v$ into a "one-sided pool": a family of pairwise disjoint finite étale closed subschemes of the two-chart model of $X_1(Mp)$ over a discrete valuation ring with residue characteristic $p$, all contained in the maximal smooth open $U$, all meeting each geometric fibre on the $\varepsilon$-side, and disjoint from $\varepsilon$, from $\varepsilon' = \sigma \circ \varepsilon$ and from the $\sigma$-translates of one another. It is used by [`ModularCurve.XOneP.exists_oneSidedPool_smoothLocus_twoChartModel_x1_mul`](thm.html#ModularCurve.XOneP.exists_oneSidedPool_smoothLocus_twoChartModel_x1_mul).
